# Review-gate integrity.
#
# The `Review Gate` check is itself defined by workflow files in this
# directory. `pull_request` runs the workflow **from the pull request**, so an
# author who edits `review-gate.yml` is judged by their own edited version and
# can remove the Greptile requirement. CODEOWNERS does not fix that on its own —
# it is the enforcement half of the mitigation:
#
#   1. Branch protection on `main` must enable
#      "Require a pull request before merging" →
#      "Require review from Code Owners".
#   2. This file must then list the maintainer for every path that can change
#      the gate or the merge policy.
#
# Without (1) these entries are advisory only. See
# docs/greptile-cost-policy.md §"Who can change the gate".
#
# If the team grows, replace the individual with a team handle (for example
# `@dlitorja/ci-owners`). A single-maintainer repo cannot self-approve, so the
# owner must review workflow changes from a second account or accept the
# documented risk.

# The gate, its helpers, and every workflow that can gate a deploy.
